        "key": "E",
        "text": "3"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "A",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Count the squares",
        "body": "Going around the board the pictures repeat in the order gift, clover, star, tree. So every group of 4 squares in a row along the path has exactly one star.\n\nCount all the squares of the board: there are 36. That is $36 \\div 4 = 9$ groups, so there were 9 stars.\n\n**Answer: (A) 9**"
      }
    ],
